UX audit wave 2 (#103, ADR-0013). Settings show only what works in this deployment: the memory switch needs memories to
be usable (the opt-out permission alone kept it visible with memories off), shared links need sharing enabled, revoking
user keys needs an endpoint that takes them, and the badge/tool switches need agent tool capabilities. A reply whose
content is a provider error gets a labelled «إعادة المحاولة» button and no read-aloud, fork or feedback actions (the
error arrives as a content part, so `message.error` alone missed it). On phones the configured footer (the trust notice)
shows above the composer of the welcome screen, because upstream hides the footer below 640 px.

